Patch summary:
Backport nine upstream minigbm fixes (chromiumos/platform/minigbm main) onto
the pinned Android 16 QPR2 base, for the guest's gralloc and its virtio-gpu
backends:

- cros_gralloc rejects imported handles with zero or more than DRV_MAX_PLANES
  planes (72b58f5), a reserved region smaller than the buffer metadata it
  holds (d6fd05d) and a layerCount of 0 (f4578b6), and no longer reads a
  buffer name past its maximum size (d40d201).
- A failed import destroys the bo it imported instead of leaking it
  (9ab051f).
- A failed multi-plane import no longer closes a GEM handle another bo still
  holds (a2d42f0).
- The virgl backend computes emulated NV12/YV12 layouts in 64 bits and fails
  buffers whose sizes would wrap in 32 bits, instead of creating a resource
  smaller than its strides imply (42d3332). The resource size check uses
  getpagesize(), as external-minigbm-upstream-stability.patch does for the
  size itself.
- The virgl bind flags are unsigned, so they no longer shift into the sign
  bit (96fcdc4).
- drv_get_os_option takes a one-character property value (6e6b465).

The upstream unit tests for the virgl changes are left out: this base has no
virtgpu_virgl_unittest.cc.

